<Project>

  <!--
    Build identity for every project in the solution.

    WHY THIS EXISTS: `dist\` and `C:\Program Files\MonkMode\` are two separate live
    installs, and both sat on a STALE build for two days after a fix shipped with nothing
    at all flagging the drift. The exes carry the inherited Cold Turkey FileVersion
    (0.7.0.0), so Windows' own properties dialog answers "which build is this?" wrongly,
    and `monkmode version` could only offer the release constant plus the file timestamp -
    which cannot distinguish two builds of the same release.

    So the CLI is stamped with the COMMIT it was built from. Both values are plain
    properties with safe fallbacks, so a bare `dotnet build` still works and still
    produces a byte-stable stamp (no incremental-build churn):

      SourceRevisionId    the git short SHA. tools\build-dist.ps1 passes it from
                          `git rev-parse` on the repo it is building; a developer build
                          leaves it "dev".
      MonkModeBuiltUtc    ISO-8601 UTC build instant, passed by the same script. Empty on
                          a developer build, and `monkmode version` then falls back to the
                          exe's own last-write time (which Copy-Item preserves, so a
                          deployed copy still reports when it was BUILT).

    Deliberately NOT a timestamp evaluated here: $([System.DateTime]::UtcNow) would differ
    on every evaluation, so the generated source would change on every build and force a
    recompile of the CLI (and the test project through it) every single time.

    The stamp is consumed by MonkMode.vbproj's StampBuildInfo target, which generates the
    BuildStamp module. These four VB projects set GenerateAssemblyInfo=false (they keep
    hand-written My Project\AssemblyInfo.vb files), so an AssemblyInformationalVersion /
    AssemblyMetadata attribute would never be emitted - a generated source file is the one
    mechanism that works here.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <SourceRevisionId Condition="'$(SourceRevisionId)' == ''">dev</SourceRevisionId>
    <MonkModeBuiltUtc Condition="'$(MonkModeBuiltUtc)' == ''"></MonkModeBuiltUtc>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
